User Guide: AquaStream360 Cost Calculator

1. Introduction
What is the Cost Calculator?
The Cost Calculator is a tool  within AquaStream360 that helps users edit network elements cost data, estimate the capital and operational costs of water distribution networks. It enables budgeting, cost comparisons, long-term financial planning, and even environmental impact assessments for network materials.
________________________________________
2. Overview of the Cost Calculator
What It Does
The module allows users to:
1.	Access and modify cost database for pipes, pumps, tanks, and valves
2.	Automatically calculate overall network costs
3.	Estimate greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions
Supported Components
•	Pipes: Different diameters and materials
•	Pumps: Various power ratings
•	Pressure Reducing Valves (PRVs): Various sizes
•	Tanks: Different storage volumes
•	Greenhouse Gas Emissions: Based on material types
________________________________________
3. Getting Started
Launching the Module
1.	Open AquaStream360 and select the Cost Calculator module
2.	Load a water network model (.INP file)
3.	Review default cost values
4.	Customize costs if needed
5.	Run the analysis
First-Time Setup
1.	Load your network model else an example network will be used
2.	Explore default costs
3.	Make adjustments to reflect local pricing
4.	Calculate initial network costs
5.	Export results for reference
________________________________________
4. Main Interface Components
4.1 Cost Type Panel
•	Select a component type: Pipes, Pumps, PRVs, Tanks, or GHG
•	Active selection is highlighted for clarity
•	Quickly switch between components to review or edit costs
4.2 Main Data Table
•	Displays component-specific cost details
•	Editable cells for adjustments
•	Columns vary depending on component type (diameter, volume, power, etc.)
•	Automatic validation ensures numbers are reasonable
4.3 Control Buttons
•	Clear Table: Remove displayed data temporarily
•	Restore Defaults: Reset to original values
•	Import Network: Load a new network
•	Show Network: Visualize the layout
•	Calculate Cost: Compute total network cost
•	Calculate GHG: Estimate greenhouse gas emissions
•	Local Currency: Convert results to local currency
•	Graph: Visualize cost trends
4.4 Status & Information Panel
•	Displays editing status, calculation results, and currency conversion updates
________________________________________
5. Cost Database Management
5.1 Default Database
•	Preloaded with industry-standard costs
•	Includes pipes, pumps, PRVs, tanks, and GHG factors
•	Covers common materials and sizes
5.2 Customization
•	Adjust costs to match local pricing or vendor quotes
•	Click a table cell, enter new values, and changes are applied immediately
•	Automatic checks ensure numbers are valid
5.3 Database Operations
•	Restore defaults if needed (cannot be undone)
•	Database automatically backs up on closing the application
•	Separate tables for each component type
________________________________________
6. Network Cost Analysis
6.1 Calculating Costs
1.	Load your network
2.	Review and adjust costs
3.	Click Calculate Cost
4.	Results appear in a summary pop-up
6.2 Understanding Results
•	Shows costs for each component and total annualized expenditure
•	Values represent yearly costs, including installation and maintenance
•	Assumes default project lifespan and discount factors
6.3 Currency Conversion
•	Click Local Currency, enter exchange rate, and view converted totals
•	Useful for local budgeting and reporting
________________________________________
7. Data Operations & Calculations
Mathematical Tools
•	Add/Subtract: Adjust all values by a fixed amount
•	Multiply/Divide: Scale values by a factor
•	Exponent: Apply power calculations
•	Graph: Visualize cost trends
Applications
•	Adjust for inflation
•	Convert currencies
•	Test different scenarios quickly
________________________________________
8. Exporting & Sharing Results
Formats
•	Excel (.xlsx): Full report with formatting
•	CSV (.csv): Quick table export
•	Database: Optional export to PostgreSQL
Locations
•	Default: Desktop > Saved AquaStream Files
•	Option to select custom folders or network drives
File Management
•	Overwrite warnings to prevent data loss
•	Automatic date/time stamps for versioning
________________________________________
9. Greenhouse Gas (GHG) Analysis
Purpose
•	Estimate carbon footprint of network components
•	Support sustainable design and regulatory compliance
How to Run
1.	Ensure network is loaded
2.	Adjust GHG factors if needed
3.	Click Calculate GHG
4.	Results displayed in pop-up
Use Cases
•	Compare materials for low-carbon options
•	Identify high-emission components
•	Include results in environmental reports
________________________________________
10. Best Practices & Tips
Database Management
•	Keep costs updated for inflation and market changes
•	Verify units are consistent
•	Document assumptions
Analysis Workflow
1.	Load network
2.	Review defaults
3.	Customize costs
4.	Calculate
5.	Test scenarios
6.	Export and document results
Reporting
•	Include date, network version, cost database version, and assumptions
•	Show annual and total costs
•	Compare different scenarios
Common Pitfalls
•	Mixing units (inches vs. meters)
•	Using outdated exchange rates
•	Forgetting to customize costs
Advanced Features
•	Network visualization to see costly components
•	Bulk operations for rapid updates

